What is cors package?
------------------------------------------------------

The CORS package is used in backend applications (commonly with Express.js) 
to allow or control requests coming from different domains (origins).

Why CORS is Needed

Browsers follow a security rule called Same-Origin Policy.

This means:

Frontend → http://localhost:3000
Backend → http://localhost:5000

Even though both run on your computer, the browser treats them as different origins because the ports are different.

Without CORS, the browser blocks the request.

What is .env?
-----------------------------------------------------------------

An .env file is used to store environment variables in a project.
It helps keep sensitive information and configuration values separate from your main code.

Why use .env file?

Instead of writing secrets directly in code:

const password = "mysecret123";

We store them safely in .env:

DB_PASSWORD=mysecret123

Then access them in code.
